From 457d90dc9009507ae824c4853025b310640de86b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: andrew <andrew@rstltd.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:47:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] preceph: read OBS2 from column 30, fixing silently
 dropped DSB records

readbiaf() reads the OBS2 field of a Bias-SINEX record from column 29,
but the SINEX_BIAS layout puts OBS2 at column 30 -- column 29 is the
separator space:

    *BIAS SVN_ PRN STATION__ OBS1 OBS2 BIAS_START____ ...
    0     6    11  15        25   30

So obs2 comes back shifted by one: " C1" instead of "C1W". obs2[1] is
then always the leading C/L of the observation code rather than the band
digit, so the same-frequency test in the DSB branch

    if (obs1[1]!=obs2[1]) continue;

compares a digit against a letter and can never match, for any code
pair. The DSB branch is therefore unreachable in its entirety and every
DSB record in the file is skipped.

The failure is silent: readbiaf() still returns 1, readdcb() reports
success, nothing appears in the trace, and every bias that should have
come from a DSB record reads back as 0. OSB-only products are unaffected
because obs2 is unused on that path, which is likely why this went
unnoticed.

The other three offsets in the function (1, 11, 25) are correct.

Introduced in 5b59da3 when the sscanf whitespace parse was replaced with
fixed-column strncpy. Moving to fixed columns is the right fix for the
blank-SVN files that motivated it; only the OBS2 offset is short.

Reproduced with a single-record GPS DSB file (C1C-C1W = 5 ns, 103
characters so it clears the length guard): code2bias(C1C) returns 0
before this change and 5e-9*CLIGHT = 1.498962290 m after.
---
 src/preceph.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/preceph.c b/src/preceph.c
index 0777c9d2..11b262d9 100644
--- a/src/preceph.c
+++ b/src/preceph.c
@@ -480,7 +480,7 @@ static int readbiaf(const char *file, nav_t *nav)
         strncpy(bias, buff+1,  3); bias[3] ='\0';
         strncpy(prn,  buff+11, 3); prn[3]  ='\0';
         strncpy(obs1, buff+25, 3); obs1[3] ='\0';
-        strncpy(obs2, buff+29, 3); obs2[3] ='\0';
+        strncpy(obs2, buff+30, 3); obs2[3] ='\0';
         if (obs1[0]!='C') continue;  /* skip phase biases for now */
         if ((cbias=str2num(buff,70,21))==0.0) continue;
         sat=satid2no(prn);
